  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[\\dfrac{10^7}{5 \\times 10^4}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.002\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.2\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(200\\)",
    "E": "\\(2000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The numerator \\(10^7\\) contains seven factors of \\(10\\), while \\(10^4\\) in the denominator contains four. Canceling those four nonzero factors leaves three factors of \\(10\\) in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{10^7}{5\\times10^4}\n=\\frac{10\\times10\\times10}{5}\n=\\frac{1000}{5}\n=200.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(200\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
